([P1] The Realm Trade Ministry reports that talks on renewing the Corridor) Tj
T*
(Agreement are progressing well.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P2] Both sides have accepted the principle of a further term, according to) Tj
T*
(officials close to the talks.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P3] The ministry expects a renewal to be signed before the current agreement) Tj
T*
(ends.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P4] Exporters should continue to plan on the existing terms in the meantime.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P5] The notice reflects the position at the time it was written, when both) Tj
T*
(delegations had described the talks as constructive. It does not say what) Tj
T*
(remained unresolved, and it does not name the officials who briefed the) Tj
T*
(ministry. Exporters were told to keep planning on the existing terms, which was) Tj
T*
(reasonable while the agreement was still in force. The notice was not updated) Tj
T*
(after the talks changed course.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P6] The notice was written after a routine meeting between the two delegations.) Tj
T*
(It records the points they agreed and leaves the remaining questions for the) Tj
T*
(next round. It does not set a date for signature and does not describe the terms) Tj
T*
(of a further term. Exporters were expected to keep their existing bookings while) Tj
T*
(the talks continued.) Tj
